      title: 'Thanksgiving',
      passage: `Thanksgiving is one of the most important holidays in the United States, and I want to tell you how my family celebrates it.\n\nIt happens every year on the fourth Thursday of November. On this day, families come together, often travelling long distances to be with each other. My aunt drives six hours every year just to join us for dinner!\n\nThe most popular food is turkey, but we also eat mashed potatoes, vegetables, and, of course, pumpkin pie for dessert. My grandmother always makes the turkey, and it takes her almost the whole day to cook it perfectly. Before the meal, we sit around the table, and everyone says one thing they are thankful for; last year, my little cousin said he was thankful for his new puppy, which made everyone laugh.\n\nAfter lunch, some family members watch American football on television, while others help clean the kitchen. My favourite part of the day is actually the evening, when we play card games together until late at night.\n\nThe next day is called Black Friday, and many people go shopping because the shops have huge sales; some people even wait outside the shops all night to get the best deals! My mother loves Black Friday shopping, but I usually stay home and rest after all the food from the day before.\n\nThanksgiving is really a time for families to be together, eat well, and feel grateful for what they have.`,
