      passage: `Baby sea turtles hatch from their eggs on sandy beaches at night. Naturally, they use moonlight reflecting off the ocean to find their way to the sea. However, bright lights from beachside hotels and buildings can confuse the baby turtles, causing them to move towards the land instead of the water, where they often die. Scientists have discovered that changing regular white lights to special LED lights, in orange or red colours, can solve this problem. These coloured lights are far less confusing for the turtles because they are more similar to natural moonlight. Many coastal towns are now replacing their lighting with these turtle-friendly LEDs. This small change is helping to save thousands of baby turtles every year, showing that a simple solution can make a huge difference for wildlife.`,
