      passage: `Families today come in many different forms, and there is no single "normal" type of family anymore. A nuclear family consists of two parents and their children living together. A single-parent family has one parent raising the children, either alone or with support from relatives. Blended families are formed when parents with children from previous relationships come together to create a new family unit. Extended families include grandparents, aunts, uncles, and cousins, sometimes all living close together or even in the same house. There are also same-sex families, where children are raised by two parents of the same gender. Regardless of its structure, what truly matters for a family is the love, support, and care that its members give each other.`,
