      passage: `Finding the right flatmate can be just as tricky as finding the right romantic partner, which is why some housing agencies now organize events called "SpeedFlatmating". Similar to speed dating, people looking for a flatmate or a spare room sit at tables and have short, five-minute conversations with each other before moving to the next person. Participants ask questions about cleanliness, work schedules, noise levels, and hobbies, trying to find someone compatible to share a home with. Organizers say the events save time compared to meeting people individually and reduce the risk of ending up with a flatmate who has completely different habits. Many participants say they prefer this method because it feels more natural than simply reading a profile online.`,
