      passage: `Selling items on eBay can be a great way to earn extra money, but a few simple tips can help you sell faster and for a better price. First, always take clear, well-lit photos of your item from several angles, as good photos attract more buyers. Second, write a detailed and honest description, mentioning any damage or wear, since honesty builds trust with buyers. Third, research similar items to set a fair and competitive price; pricing too high can scare buyers away, while pricing too low means losing money. Fourth, respond to buyer questions quickly, as fast replies often lead to faster sales. Finally, package items carefully to avoid damage during shipping, since good reviews depend heavily on buyers receiving items in perfect condition.`,
