      title: 'The Ig Nobel Prizes',
      passage: `The Ig Nobel Prizes are awards given every year for scientific research that "first makes people laugh, and then makes them think". Unlike the serious Nobel Prizes, the Ig Nobel ceremony is full of humour, held at a famous university, with real Nobel Prize winners often handing out the awards. Past winners have studied strange topics, such as why woodpeckers don't get headaches, whether cats can be both a solid and a liquid, and why people slip on banana skins. Although the topics sound silly, the research is genuinely scientific and often published in serious academic journals. The organizers believe that unusual, curious research can lead to important discoveries, and that science should be able to make people smile as well as think.`,
