      passage: `Divorce is often associated with conflict and bitterness, but an increasing number of former couples are choosing to remain friends after separating, especially when children are involved. Experts say that maintaining a friendly relationship after divorce requires both people to let go of blame and focus on cooperation, particularly regarding parenting responsibilities. Some divorced couples even continue to celebrate holidays together as a family, prioritizing their children's emotional stability over their own personal feelings. However, psychologists caution that staying friends is not the right choice for everyone; in situations involving abuse or serious betrayal, maintaining contact can be harmful rather than helpful. For couples without children, some choose to stay friends simply because they shared many years of history together and don't want to lose that connection completely. Ultimately, whether or not to stay friends after divorce depends heavily on the specific circumstances and the emotional health of both individuals involved.`,
