      title: 'AI Boomers vs AI Doomers',
      passage: `As artificial intelligence continues to develop rapidly, public opinion has broadly split into two camps, sometimes nicknamed "AI boomers" and "AI doomers". AI boomers are generally optimistic, believing that artificial intelligence will bring enormous benefits to humanity, from curing diseases and solving climate change to freeing people from repetitive, boring work. They argue that fear of new technology has always existed throughout history, and that society ultimately adapts and benefits in the long run. AI doomers, on the other hand, worry about serious risks, including mass unemployment, the spread of misinformation, and even the possibility that highly advanced AI systems could eventually act in ways that are difficult for humans to control or predict. Between these two extremes, many experts occupy a more cautious middle ground, acknowledging AI's potential benefits while calling for stronger regulation and safety research to help manage its risks responsibly.`,
