      title: 'What Type of Accommodation Best Suits You?',
      passage: `Choosing the right type of accommodation, whether for a holiday or a longer stay abroad, depends heavily on your personal priorities, budget, and travel style. If privacy and comfort are your main concerns, a hotel or private apartment rental might suit you best, offering consistency and independence, though usually at a higher price. If you are travelling on a tight budget and enjoy meeting other travellers, a hostel could be ideal, since shared rooms and communal spaces naturally encourage social interaction. For those seeking a more authentic, local experience, staying with a host family through a homestay programme allows deeper cultural immersion and often includes home-cooked meals. Meanwhile, house-sitting, where you stay in someone's home for free in exchange for looking after their pets or property, has become increasingly popular among long-term travellers seeking to reduce costs. Ultimately, there is no single "best" option; the right choice always depends on what each individual traveller values most during their trip.`,
